  "preview_story": {
    "title": "The Footprints Led In. Nobody Came Out.",
    "story_id": "hinterkaifeck_1922_review",
    "source": "inbox/hinterkaifeck_1922.txt",
    "mode": "inbox-script",
    "true_story": true,
    "setting": "Bavaria, Germany, March 1922",
    "render_style": "classic",
    "visual_mode": "classic",
    "narrator_voice": "am_adam",
    "hook_text": "FOOTPRINTS IN. NONE OUT.",
    "scenes": [
      {
        "narration": "Someone walked out of the frozen woods and straight toward their farmhouse. But the footprints never led back out.",
        "image_prompt": "A trail of footprints in the snow leading toward a dark isolated farmhouse at night",
        "project_asset_ids": [
          "snow_farmhouse_footprints_concept"
        ],
        "asset_frame": "none",
        "sfx": "footsteps_snow",
        "image_prompt_2": "A moonlit farmhouse behind a close trail of snow footprints and a tall shadow on the right",
        "project_asset_ids_a": [
          "snow_farmhouse_footprints_concept"
        ],
        "project_asset_ids_b": [
          "moonlit_farmhouse_footprints_shadow"
        ]
      },
      {
        "narration": "That was the story a Bavarian farmer reportedly told in March nineteen twenty-two. Then came more strange warnings.",
        "image_prompt": "A snowy isolated farmhouse with a single warm window glowing in the night",
        "project_asset_ids": [
          "snow_farmhouse_warm_window"
        ],
        "asset_frame": "none",
        "sfx": "winter_wind"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Footsteps supposedly echoed through the attic. A newspaper appeared that nobody recognized. And a house key was missing.",
        "image_prompt": "A dark human silhouette standing in a wooden attic with light through slats",
        "project_asset_ids": [
          "attic_shadow_figure"
        ],
        "asset_frame": "documentary",
        "sfx": "floor_creak"
      },
      {
        "narration": "On March thirty-first, six people were murdered at Hinterkaifeck. Four bodies were found in the barn, and two inside the farmhouse, including the newly arrived maid.",
        "image_prompt": "Investigators with a lantern examining a wooden barn at a rural farmhouse",
        "project_asset_ids": [
          "barn_investigation_lantern_illustration"
        ],
        "asset_frame": "documentary",
        "sfx": "door_creak"
      },
      {
        "narration": "A mattock, later recovered on the property, was identified as the likely weapon. But the strangest detail came afterward.",
        "image_prompt": "An old mattock tool standing in a dark barn, wooden handle and iron blade",
        "project_asset_ids": [
          "barn_mattock_tool"
        ],
        "asset_frame": "documentary",
        "sfx": "clock_ticking"
      },
      {
        "narration": "There were indications somebody had stayed after the killings. The animals had apparently been tended, and smoke was reported from the chimney.",
        "image_prompt": "A remote snowy farmhouse with smoke rising from the chimney at night",
        "project_asset_ids": [
          "farmhouse_chimney_smoke"
        ],
        "asset_frame": "none",
        "sfx": "winter_wind"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Was the murderer hiding nearby before the attack? Or were these clues misunderstood?",
        "image_prompt": "An imagined hooded intruder crouching in a wooden attic, a speculative illustration",
        "project_asset_ids": [
          "hooded_figure_attic"
        ],
        "asset_frame": "none",
        "sfx": "eerie_chime"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Investigators never established who killed the six residents. More than one hundred years later, who was there remains a mystery.",
        "image_prompt": "A trail of deep footprints through snow and forest toward an isolated farmhouse",
        "project_asset_ids": [
          "snow_footprint_trail"
        ],
        "asset_frame": "none",
        "sfx": "winter_wind"
      }
    ],
    "fact_ledger": [
      "Six people were killed in March 1922. The case remains unsolved.",
      "Footprints, attic sounds and post-crime occupation are reported details, not proof of a known killer."
    ],
    "sources": [
